    // true. Dart's int is also exactly 64-bit two's complement on the VM and WRAPS
    // (int64max + 1 is int64min), which a JS double cannot represent at all - it said
    // 9223372036854776000.
    //
    // Both are fixed by putting the type ON the value, the way java-interpreter.abnf's
    // {__flo} box and go-interpreter.abnf's sized integers already do. The invariant, in
    // BOTH halves of this language (abnf/jsrtdart.go implements exactly these rules):
    //
    //     a plain number    ==  an int whose value is exact in a double (|v| <= 2^53)
    //     an {__sz} box     ==  an int outside that range (w = 64, u = false, always)
    //     an {__flo} box    ==  a double
